    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a> proclaimed himself <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> in 929, rivalling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> became the largest city of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosque-cathedral-of-cordoba">Great Mosque</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madinat-al-zahra">Madinat al-Zahra</a> and celebrated libraries.</li><li>After the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almanzor">Almanzor</a>’s death, civil war from 1009 broke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>, which was abolished in 1031.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 958 the deposed King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-i-of-leon">Sancho I of León</a>, known as ‘the Fat’, travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> with his grandmother Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toda-of-pamplona">Toda of Navarre</a> to be treated for obesity by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasdai-ibn-shaprut">Hasdai ibn Shaprut</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

